/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Write the multiplicand as A = an−1...a0 and the multiplier as B = bn−1...b0.
   - P = Σj=0n−1 (Σi=0n−1 aibj 2i) 2j = Σi=0n−1Σj=0n−1 aibj 2i+j
   - Here P is the 2n-bit product; ai is bit i of A; bj is bit j of B; ppij = aibj is one partial product bit; 2i+j fixes its column.
   - A 4×4 array needs 16 AND gates to form pp00 to pp33.
   - The Braun multiplier is the plain unsigned array just described.
   - A first delay estimate: the slowest signal passes about n − 1 adders down the rows and about n − 1 adders along the final ripple row, so tp ≈ tAND + 2(n−1)·tFA, where tFA is one adder delay.
   - Signed numbers use two's complement.
   - Generate the low bits normally: aibj for i,j ≤ n−2.
   - PBW = Σi=0n−2Σj=0n−2 aibj2i+j + Σj=0n−2 NOT(an−1bj)2n−1+j + Σi=0n−2 NOT(aibn−1)2n−1+i + an−1bn−122n−2 + 22n−1 + 2n
   - Here PBW is the signed product modulo 22n; NOT(x) is 1−x; the two added powers are the two 1 bits; all powers of 2 are bit positions in the final product.
*/
